Description: archive: use chrootarchive over plain archive package (additional hardening)
 Backport the upstream "use chrootarchive over plain archive package" change
 (a49ad4be, cherry-picked from 25aee24cbd), which upstream describes as
 "Just as additional hardening".  It is NOT the fix for CVE-2025-11395: the
 authoritative fix is the container-libs security update GHSA-3gcv-x57j-xqxv,
 i.e. containers/storage >= 1.62.1 and containers/image >= 5.39.3 (or the
 consolidated backports acbb1e7 / bdae767).  This package builds against
 containers/storage 1.55.1 and containers/image 5.32.2, so the podman load
 OCI-archive unpack path in containers/image is unchanged by this patch.
 .
 Adapted for the 5.2 source layout: podman volume import extracts through
 utils.UntarToFileSystem in this version, so that call site is hardened as
 well.
 .
 The pkg/domain/infra/tunnel/images.go hunk of the upstream commit is
 deliberately omitted: upstream reverted that line in fd07b9c6e because
 chrootarchive cannot work for the rootless podman-remote client
 ("creating mount namespace before pivot: operation not permitted"), which
 broke podman-remote save -f oci-dir/docker-dir.
